---
import data from '../site-data.json';
import catalog from '../catalog.json';
import '../style.css';
const sample=data.posts.filter(p=>p.year>='2023').slice(0,72);
const groups=[{name:'2023–2026',n:2342,posts:sample}];
const visuals=data.posts.filter(p=>p.image).length;
const modes=[['timeline','Timeline'],['topics','Topics'],['response','Response map'],['words','Writing & response'],['rank','Ranking'],['palette','Colour'],['format','Format']];
const safeJSON=JSON.stringify({...data,sprite:{cols:data.sprite.cols,rows:data.sprite.rows}}).replaceAll('<','\\u003c');
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="theme-color" content="#10253f"/><meta name="description" content="Riad Meddeb’s LinkedIn presence: explore 5,413 archive records through their images, topics and public response."/><title>Riad Meddeb · LinkedIn presence</title><link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Crect width='32' height='32' rx='8' fill='%2300689d'/%3E%3Ctext x='16' y='23' text-anchor='middle' fill='white' font-size='22'%3ER%3C/text%3E%3C/svg%3E"/></head><body>
<a class="skip" href="#atlas">Skip to post atlas</a><header><a class="brand" href="#">RIAD MEDDEB <span>/ LINKEDIN</span></a><nav><a href="#atlas">Post atlas</a><a href="#report">Analysis</a><a href="#method">Method</a></nav></header><main>
<section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">2010 — October 2026</div><h1>Riad Meddeb’s<br/><em>LinkedIn presence</em></h1><p>The topics he covers, how his writing has changed, and which posts attract reactions and comments.</p><div class="hero-bottom"><div><strong>{data.posts.length.toLocaleString()}</strong> archive records <span>·</span> <strong>{visuals.toLocaleString()}</strong> linked visuals</div><a href="Riad_Meddeb_Rebuilt_Dataset.xlsx">Download the rebuilt dataset ↗</a></div></section>
<section id="atlas" class="atlas-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / Explore the posts</span><h2>Explore the post archive</h2></div><p>Each tile is an archive record.<br/>Switch between original posts and reposts.</p></div>
<div class="post-atlas" id="post-atlas"><div class="atlas-controls" id="atlas-controls"><div class="view-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Atlas layout">{modes.map(([id,title])=><button data-mode={id} aria-pressed={id==='timeline'}>{title}</button>)}</div><div class="filters"><label class="search">Search posts<input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Search full captions…"/></label><div class="year-filter"><span>Year</span><div role="group" aria-label="Year">{['recent','2023','2024','2025','2026','earlier','all'].map(year=><button data-year={year} aria-pressed={year==='recent'}>{year==='recent'?'Recent':year==='earlier'?'Earlier':year==='all'?'All history':year}</button>)}</div></div><label>Topic<select id="topic" aria-label="Topic"><option value="all">All topics</option>{Object.keys(data.colors).map(topic=><option>{topic}</option>)}</select></label><div class="year-filter"><span>Record</span><div role="group" aria-label="Record type">{[['all','All'],['original','Originals'],['repost','Reposts']].map(([id,label])=><button data-kind={id} aria-pressed={id==='all'}>{label}</button>)}</div></div><label id="rank-control" hidden>Rank by<select id="metric" aria-label="Rank by"><option value="reactions">Reactions</option><option value="comments">Comments</option></select></label><button id="reset" hidden>Clear filters</button></div></div>
<div class="atlas-caption"><p id="view-description">See the visual balance across named topics.</p><span id="atlas-count" role="status">2,342 records · 2023–2026</span></div>
<div class="atlas-window" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable post visualization"><div id="atlas-stage" class="atlas-stage static-atlas" style={`--atlas-image:url("${data.sprite.src}");--atlas-size:${data.sprite.cols*100}% ${data.sprite.rows*100}%`}>
{groups.map(group=><><h3 class="static-group">{group.name}<small>{group.n} posts</small></h3>{group.posts.map(p=><button class="post-icon" data-id={p.id} aria-label={`Post ${p.index}, ${p.date}: ${p.title}. ${p.reactions??'Unknown'} reactions, ${p.comments??'Unknown'} comments`} style={`--topic:${data.colors[p.topic]||'#748b99'}`}>
{p.image?<span class="post-thumb" aria-hidden="true" data-post-id={p.id} style={`background-position:${p.sprite[0]/(data.sprite.cols-1)*100}% ${p.sprite[1]/(data.sprite.rows-1)*100}%`}></span>:<span class="no-image">No<br/>visual</span>}<span class="post-index">{p.index}</span></button>)}</>)}
</div></div>
<div class="atlas-inspector" aria-live="polite"><span id="inspector-index" class="inspector-index"></span><div><strong id="inspector-title">Select an image to read its caption and inspect its counters.</strong><small id="inspector-meta">Image proportions are preserved.</small></div><button id="inspect-post" hidden>Read post ↗</button></div>
<details id="missing" class="missing" hidden><summary></summary><div></div></details>
<details id="text-index" class="text-index"><summary>Browse this selection as an accessible text list</summary><div></div></details></div></section>
<section id="report"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / Read the analysis</span><h2>Patterns behind the posts</h2></div><p>Topic comparisons, writing patterns and public response, with the source posts one click away.</p></div><div class="analysis-nav"><label>Go to analysis<select id="analysis-jump"><option value="">Choose a chart</option>{catalog.map(f=><option value={f.id}>{f.title}</option>)}</select></label><span>{catalog.length} analyses</span></div>
{catalog.map(f=><article class="figure" id={f.id}><div class="figureheader"><span class="eyebrow">{f.chapter} / {String(f.number).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h2>{f.title}</h2></div><div class="figuretext"><p>{f.analysis}</p></div><div class="chart-placeholder" aria-label="Chart loads when visible"></div><details class="figure-note"><summary>Sample and interpretation</summary><p>{f.note}</p></details></article>)}
</section>
<section id="method" class="method"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Sources & files</span><h2>What the record can tell us</h2><p>The export contains 3,910 unique share records and 1,503 instant reposts. The archive includes all 5,413 records. The initial view covers 2023–2026; choose Earlier or All history to explore the rest.</p><p>All 2,342 links in the 2023–2026 scope were checked: 2,312 pages were recovered and 30 remain unavailable. The Shares file includes 660 verified original posts and 170 reposts. Earlier records retain export text and dates, with no claim of live verification. Export dates have no declared timezone.</p><p>Response charts use original-post counters only. Missing counts remain unknown. Writing features are computed from recovered original captions. Topic and approach charts use the previously classified subset, identified beside each chart; new records are marked Unclassified. Counts are cumulative reactions and comments, not reach or engagement rates.</p><p>One main image or cover is linked where recovered. Images are stored once and reused across records. Public comments in the workbook are a partial sample. Verification: 7 October 2026.</p><div class="downloads"><a href="Riad_Meddeb_Rebuilt_Dataset.xlsx">Full spreadsheet ↗</a><a href="Shares.csv">All shares · CSV ↗</a><a href="Instant_Reposts.csv">Instant reposts · CSV ↗</a><a href="Posts_2023_2026.csv">2023–2026 shares · CSV ↗</a><a href="Image_Manifest.csv">Image manifest ↗</a><a href="Annual_Coverage.csv">Annual coverage ↗</a></div></section><footer>Built from the account export, public pages and signed-in browser verification.</footer></main>
<dialog id="post-dialog" aria-labelledby="post-title"><button class="close">Close ×</button><div class="dialoggrid"><div id="dialog-image"></div><div><span id="post-meta" class="eyebrow"></span><h2 id="post-title"></h2><p id="post-topic"></p><div id="post-counters" class="counters"></div><p id="post-caption" class="caption"></p><p id="post-check" class="counter-note"></p><div id="post-links" class="downloads"></div></div></div></dialog>
<noscript><p>The atlas images and analysis text are available without JavaScript. Enable JavaScript for filters and post dialogs, or download the spreadsheet for full captions.</p></noscript>
<script id="atlas-data" type="application/json" is:inline set:html={safeJSON}></script><script>import '../app.js';</script>
</body></html>
